# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example  —  copy to .env and fill in real values.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️  CRITICAL SAFETY RULES — read before editing  ⚠️
#
# 1. NEVER commit .env. It is listed in .gitignore; keep it that way.
#    Rotate any credential that accidentally lands in git history.
#
# 2. NEVER point BASE_URL at a production host. The test suite WILL
#    create data, submit forms, and click destructive buttons. Allowed
#    targets: a LOCAL dev server (http://localhost:<port> / 127.0.0.1)
#    or a staging / dedicated QA environment — NOTHING customer-facing,
#    EVER. If a BASE_URL host carries a `prod`/`production` marker at a WORD
#    BOUNDARY (not a bare substring — `product`/`reproduction` do NOT trip it),
#    the prod-guard stops the run — don't rely on that, verify yourself.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sites under test — one BASE_URL_<SITE> per entry in
# specs/_context/app.context.md `sites:` block.
# MUST be staging or a dedicated QA env — never prod.
# The prod-guard (CLAUDE.md §Environment) screens EVERY exported BASE_URL_* var
# (not just BASE_URL_APP) and word-boundary-matches each host for "prod" before any
# run. Two layers, no PreToolUse hook: (1) a best-effort shell safety-print the agent
# runs on the CLI-driving/authoring paths, and (2) an ENFORCED `globalSetup` prod-guard
# (`scripts/prod-guard.ts` in playwright.config.ts) that applies the same logic and
# throws before any browser opens — so a bare `npx playwright test` is covered too.
# QA_ALLOW_PROD=1 overrides the prod-marker check ONLY (placeholder / empty-target
# refusals have no env escape — the fix is editing this file). Residual limit: a prod host with no telltale name
# (e.g. www.acme.com) still can't be auto-detected, so keep every BASE_URL_* on
# staging/QA yourself and load .env with `set -a` so the vars are exported for the loop.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Customer-facing storefront (site id: app).
# Ships as CHANGEME: prod-guard.sh + prod-guard.ts FAIL-CLOSED on an empty/placeholder
# host, so the very first guard run REFUSES until you set a real staging/QA target here — a
# green guard against a host you never chose is worse than a STOP. Replace with your URL.
BASE_URL_APP=CHANGEME

# Local is a first-class target: BASE_URL_APP=http://localhost:3000 passes both
# prod-guards by design (localhost never matches a prod marker). Start the dev server
# yourself, or uncomment the webServer block in playwright.config.ts so Playwright
# starts/stops it per run.

# Back-office / admin (site id: admin). COMMENTED OUT on purpose: playwright.config.ts
# activates the `admin` project (and its setup dep) whenever BASE_URL_ADMIN is truthy, so
# leaving a placeholder host here makes a fresh `npx playwright test` spin up an admin
# project pointed at a bogus URL. Single-site is the zero-config default — uncomment and
# set a REAL admin staging host only when you actually add an admin site.
# BASE_URL_ADMIN=https://admin.staging.example.com

# Backwards-compat: single-site forks can keep using BASE_URL; the
# generator and the seed fixtures fall back to it when BASE_URL_APP is unset.
# BASE_URL=https://staging.example.com

# Standard user — created ahead of time in the staging environment.
QA_USER_EMAIL=
QA_USER_PASSWORD=

# Admin user — for permission / role tests.
QA_ADMIN_EMAIL=
QA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Named persona referenced by the EXAMPLE YAML specs (planner.md's `alice@example.com`).
# Intentionally password-only: emails may be inline literals in a spec's `data:` block,
# but passwords are ALWAYS `password_env:` references, never inline — so a persona needs
# only its `_PW` here (there is no paired `QA_ALICE_EMAIL` by design). Real suites use the
# QA_USER_*/QA_ADMIN_* accounts above; this exists so the shipped example specs resolve.
QA_ALICE_PW=

# ── Seed API (test-data-seed skill) — fill in when you wire API seeding ──
# The seed fixtures read these from .env (the only env file playwright.config.ts
# loads). QA_ADMIN_TOKEN is a LIVE admin bearer token — a HUMAN puts it here
# (agents are not granted write access to .env — a write needs explicit human
# approval, as .env is outside the settings.json write-allowlist); rotate it if it ever lands in git
# history. Leaving these unset while a seed fixture runs would POST to
# "undefined/admin/users" with "Bearer undefined" — declare the app's real
# equivalents when you wire the seed adapter.
# API_URL=https://staging-api.example.com
# QA_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# QA_RUN_ID=            # optional run tag the seed fixtures use for teardown-by-tag ("test-run-<id>"); defaults to "local"

# Optional: CI-only. Issued once via `claude setup-token` on a logged-in
# machine. Consumes Max subscription quota in CI.
# Leave blank for local dev — `claude` uses the OAuth keychain instead.
# Never run `claude` with `--bare` if you want subscription billing — it forces
# API-key auth and ignores the OAuth keychain.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# ── Optional run-time toggles (usually set inline, e.g. `QA_KEEP_VIDEO=1 npx …`) ──
# These are switches, not secrets — most people pass them per-command rather than
# persist them here. Documented so you know they exist:
#   QA_KEEP_VIDEO=1     keep the .webm even when a test PASSES (default is
#                       retain-on-failure). For confirming a freshly-authored spec
#                       drives the flow you meant; the generator sets it on a new
#                       spec's final run. Watch artifacts/test-results/<id>/video.webm,
#                       then delete artifacts/. NEVER set this in the nightly/CI —
#                       it defeats the cheap-replay design and piles up green videos.
#   QA_RUN_QUARANTINE=1 run the @quarantine lane that default runs skip.
#   QA_RUN_OF_RECORD=1  refresh artifacts/last-run.json (set by /qa-warden:run mode=smoke; the
#                       nightly sets it via CI). Leave unset for ad-hoc/agent runs.
#   QA_ALLOW_PROD=1     override the prod-guard's prod-MARKER check only. Do NOT persist this here.
#   QA_LOCALE=de-DE     browser locale (default en-US). Match the app's locale so string
#                       oracles pass; changing it means re-validating every
#                       text_visible/error_shown literal and re-baselining aria snapshots.
#   QA_TZ=Europe/Berlin timezone (default UTC, pinned for deterministic dates).
#   QA_WORKERS=2        cap parallel workers for staging capacity; number or '50%'.
# Uncomment ONLY if you truly want one always-on locally:
# QA_KEEP_VIDEO=1

# ── Walled-staging access (all optional — unset = knob off) ──
# Each maps to a `use:` knob in playwright.config.ts that stays a no-op until set.
# QA_BASIC_AUTH_USER=   # basic-auth wall in front of staging (sent only after a 401 challenge)
# QA_BASIC_AUTH_PASS=   # its password
# QA_EXTRA_HEADER_NAME=X-QA-Bypass   # one extra header on every request (WAF/staging-gate bypass)
# QA_EXTRA_HEADER_VALUE=             # its value — two envs, no "name:value" parsing to get wrong
# QA_PROXY_SERVER=http://proxy.internal:3128   # corporate egress proxy to reach the walled staging
# QA_CLIENT_CERT_ORIGIN=       # origin that demands an mTLS client certificate
# QA_CLIENT_CERT_PATH=         # path to the client cert (PEM)
# QA_CLIENT_KEY_PATH=          # path to its private key
# QA_CLIENT_CERT_PASSPHRASE=   # key passphrase, if any — a credential: never commit

# ── Auth beyond form login (only for sites whose app.context auth_mode needs them) ──
# QA_TOTP_SECRET=       # TOTP seed (auth_mode: totp) — the base32 secret behind the QR code
#                       # shown at 2FA enrolment on STAGING. The setup file computes the code
#                       # with the `otpauth` lib. A credential: never commit, rotate on leak.
# QA_AUTH_STATE_MAX_AGE_HOURS=24   # age (hours) before a pre-minted storageState
#                       # (auth_mode: manual) draws a setup WARN. Hard-FAIL is separate: any
#                       # cookie past `expires` / JWT past `exp` fails setup outright.

# ── Agent budgets ──
# HEALER_TURN_BUDGET=14 # hard turn limit per failure for the healer subagent (CLAUDE.md
#                       # §Escalation rules). Default 14 when unset. Raise it only deliberately:
#                       # the cap is what stops a healer burning tokens on an un-healable
#                       # product defect instead of filing a bug and reverting its patch.
